---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import WhatsAppButton from "../components/WhatsAppButton.astro";
import { site, towns } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="South Coast"
  description="Local proof: FactSmith Sites work for owner-operated businesses on the KZN Hibiscus Coast. Businesses elsewhere are welcome too."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-ink-900">South Coast</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-700">
      We build for owner-operated businesses across South Africa. The Hibiscus Coast is home: our first
      clients are here, and Sharon looks after South Coast enquiries in person. Lodges, B&Bs, tutors,
      trades and professionals, where the website is clearly overdue for a rebuild.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Where we know the ground best</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {
        towns.map((town) => (
          <li class="rounded-full bg-sea-50 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-sea-800">{town}</li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500">Elsewhere in South Africa, or abroad? Message Emilio.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">A rebuild is worth it when</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-2 text-ink-700">
      <li>The site breaks or scrolls sideways on a phone</li>
      <li>There is no tap-to-call and no WhatsApp button</li>
      <li>You cannot change the site yourself (dead WordPress, old `.htm` tables)</li>
      <li>Facebook or Airbnb is doing the real work and the `.co.za` is an embarrassment</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <WhatsAppButton label="South Coast: send Sharon your site" />
      <WhatsAppButton label="Elsewhere: message Emilio" href={site.emilio.whatsappLink} message={site.emilio.whatsappMessage} class="ml-3" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
